<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Benedict IX</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1012–c. 1056</span> · Also known as Benedict IX</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benedict IX, born Theophylactus of Tusculum, was pope three times between 1032 and 1048, the only man to hold the office on more than one occasion. A nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-benedict-viii">Benedict VIII</a> and John XIX, he was made pope young by his family, the counts of Tusculum. He was driven out, sold the office to Gregory VI in 1045, and returned briefly before being removed for good in 1048.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-benedict-ix.jpg" alt="Pope Benedict IX" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tassin et Toustain. G.Garitan pour le versement et les modifications . · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_abbaye_COlombs_Benoist_IX_17002.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
